# Purpose

This document defines the Software-as-a-Service (SaaS) engineering standards for the hubIO platform.

Its purpose is to establish architectural principles that enable hubIO to operate as a scalable multi-tenant business platform while preserving tenant isolation, operational flexibility, and long-term product evolution.

---

# Scope

This standard defines:

* SaaS philosophy
* Multi-tenant architecture
* Organization ownership
* Product scalability
* Platform governance
* SaaS evolution

It intentionally excludes subscription models, billing implementation, authentication technologies, pricing strategy, and infrastructure deployment, which are defined by their respective Engineering Standards.

---

# Constitutional Interpretation

This document extends the hubIO Engineering Constitution.

It applies constitutional engineering principles to the SaaS product model, ensuring business capabilities remain scalable, isolated, and maintainable across every customer organization.

